Do not introduce purple, blue, green, teal, red, grey, beige, cream, pastel palettes or any other independent colour.

Do not create a blue-and-purple technology aesthetic.

Do not use generic multicoloured gradients.

Do not introduce different colours for individual categories, icons, badges, avatars or status indicators.

For subtle effects, use transparency or opacity variations of the approved colours rather than introducing new hues.

Keep the visual identity recognisable and consistent from the first screen to the footer.

The finished page should clearly look like it belongs to the yellow, berry-pink and burnt-orange Build Buds brand.

